:13:14Z"},"comments":11,"created_at":"2025-02-20T18:03:56Z","updated_at":"2025-04-02T12:44:05Z","closed_at":"2025-04-02T12:42:57Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in v4.4.beta4 (Tested on Windows 10 and 11)\n- Reproducible in v4.4.beta1.mono (on Windows 11)\n- Reproducible in v4.4.dev5 (on Windows 11)\n- Not reproducible in v4.4.beta4.mono (on Debian 12)\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.beta4 - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4050 Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6103) - AMD Ryzen 7 7840HS w/ Radeon 780M Graphics (16 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\n`OS.get_stdin_type()` returns 0 on Windows when running exported project from console. (Related to the last note in [read_string_from_stdin](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_os.html#class-os-method-read-string-from-stdin) in docs). \n- Expected to return 1 (STD_HANDLE_CONSOLE). \n**STDIN was previously available** if running from Windows' command prompt.\n- **Returns 1 when running the project from the editor, which was launched with a console.**\n- Works as expected (returns 1) on Debian GNU/Linux 12 (bookworm), running exported project with --headless.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a scene with a script, which prints `OS.get_stdin_type()`, `OS.get_stdout_type()`, `OS.get_stderr_type()` on ready.\n2. Export project with Windows Desktop preset or run Godot in the same directory (with `cmd /c` or directly)\n3. Run exported project (optionally with --headless) from command prompt\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githu